(3047, 2075, 813, 8, 4065, '2026-10-02', '13:55:44', 'Post-op review', 'Acute appendicitis, uncomplicated (S/P Laparoscopic Appendectomy, Post-Op Day 14)', '', '', 'SUBJECTIVE:\nPatient presents for a scheduled 2-week post-operative follow-up following an uncomplicated laparoscopic appendectomy. Reports mild, intermittent incisional discomfort rated 1/10, managed without analgesics. Denies fever, chills, nausea, vomiting, abdominal distension, or changes in bowel habits. Tolerating a regular diet well.\n\nOBJECTIVE:\nPhysical Exam: Abdomen soft, non-tender, non-distended; normal bowel sounds present in all four quadrants.\r\n\r\nSurgical Sites: Umbilical and lower abdomen trocar port sites are clean, dry, and well-approximated with intact healing skin bridges. No erythema, warmth, induration, or purulent drainage noted.\n\nASSESSMENT:\n30-year-old male, Post-Op Day 14 status-post laparoscopic appendectomy, demonstrating expected, uncomplicated surgical wound healing and recovery.\n\nPLAN:\nActivity: Cleared for full physical activity and light exercise; resume normal heavy lifting after 2 additional weeks.\r\n\r\nDiet: Regular diet as tolerated.\r\n\r\nWound Care: Continue keeping incision sites clean and dry; standard bathing permitted.\r\n\r\nMedications: Discontinue routine post-op analgesics; use PRN Paracetamol 500 mg PO q6h only if needed for mild discomfort.\r\n\r\nFollow-up: PRN return to clinic or ER if experiencing fever (>38 °C), worsening abdominal pain, redness, swelling, or discharge from incision sites.', NULL, 'Completed', '120/80', 36.8, NULL, 70.00, 1.70, '2026-10-02 13:55:44', '2026-10-04 00:52:21'),
